// The designated file of the folder 'modselfnamed', imported by
// module_parse_dupname.cone and never compiled on its own, so the folder is
// listed in cases.toml as a support module under its own name.
//
// The folder names the module, and that name is bound in the module's own
// namespace when the import loads it, before this file is parsed. The 'mod'
// line restates the name, and a declaration is nearer than the file's first
// line, so the module takes its position from it. The function below spells
// the same name, so it is the duplicate, and the module's half of the
// diagnostic is reported at the 'mod' line.

mod modselfnamed;          //~ ErrorDupName:1 "conflicting definition"

fn modselfnamed() i64 {    //~ ErrorDupName:1 "already defined"
  1i64;
}
